From 3fab51eb0a5ce0de0f343d3561b8c5c345f84d23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lbgos <285507185+lbgos@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:13:11 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 37/46] rift_s: bound radio queue with monotonic deadline and
 HID backoff

Add per-command monotonic deadline (1500 ms, beyond the device 1000 ms
timeout) so a missing response fails the head instead of wedging the
queue. Bound send and poll transport errors (8 each) with 5 ms doubling
to 100 ms backoff so a persistent STALL cannot spin HID ioctls.

Retries resend only the unsent head with identical bytes; once sent the
head is polled, never resent. The response carries no command echo
(seqnum/busy only), so a late reply after a timeout can be misattributed
to the next command; last seq is retained to ignore duplicates and
callers must validate payload status/length.

Fail callbacks once via a shared helper; clear stays safe after timeouts.
HID -1/errno semantics unchanged; valid busy polls every tick.

Add fake-HID/fake-time tests for success pipelining, busy timeout
advance, send/poll/short backoff bounds, clear-once safety, stale seq,
and null HID expiry.

(cherry picked from commit 720d93e12eab09fb5b03c6ac1a9efce0155069a0)
---
